+``file-staged``
+    The same sparse file and the same allocator, but read by the *host* instead
+    of dereferenced by the gather kernel: the row ids are copied back to the
+    host, the rows are memcpy'd out of the mapping into a pinned staging slab,
+    and one pinned-to-device copy publishes them into the buffer the next graph
+    segment reads. This is the backend for discrete GPUs, which do not report
+    ``cudaDevAttrPageableMemoryAccessUsesHostPageTables`` and so cannot take the
+    ``file`` path at all. It trades the kernel's zero-copy dereference for a
+    device-to-host copy of the ids, a host read and a host-to-device copy, and
+    being a host round trip it has to be a CUDA-graph break; see
+    ``Qwen4ExpStagedFileEmbedding`` in ``qwen4_exp``.
